WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.569 --> 00:00:04.003
-Billionaire Mike Bloomberg
is apparently close to joining

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:05.938
the Democratic primary
as Wall Street panics

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:07.373
about the current
crop of candidates.

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:08.908
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.376
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:13.112 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:15.749
It's hard to keep track
of all the corruption

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.183
swirling around President Trump.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:19.285
But on top of the impeachment
inquiry and everything else,

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.587
there was also
this little item last week

00:00:21.587 --> 00:00:22.888
that went largely unnoticed --

00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:24.624
A judge ordered the president
of the United States

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:27.593
to pay $2 million
for misusing funds

00:00:27.593 --> 00:00:30.730
from his charity
for ridiculous purchases.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.932
-A New York judge ordering
President Trump

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:35.001
to pay $2 million for misusing

00:00:35.001 --> 00:00:36.902
Trump Foundation
charitable funds.

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:40.039
The president had vowed
never to settle the lawsuit.

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:41.574
The New York State
Attorney General

00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:43.409
alleged the president
used the charity's money

00:00:43.409 --> 00:00:46.913
to help his 2016 campaign
pay business debts,

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:49.248
even to by buy
a painting of himself.

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:52.284
-That's right.
Trump used charity money

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:55.955
to buy a painting of himself,
and this is the painting.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.590
[ Laughter ]

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.758
Look at that.

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:00.626
It looks like they hired
Jackson Pollock

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:03.296
to do a courtroom sketch.

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.031
Almost as shocking
as the settlement itself

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:06.832
was the fact that Trump
admitted wrongdoing.

00:01:06.832 --> 00:01:08.802
As part of the settlement,
Trump acknowledged

00:01:08.802 --> 00:01:11.704
in a court filing that he had
failed to follow basic laws

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.273
about how charities
should be governed.

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:14.973
In a statement
signed by Trump's attorney,

00:01:14.973 --> 00:01:17.544
the president admitted to poor
oversight of the charity.

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:18.744
And you know it must be bad

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:20.579
because Trump never apologizes
for anything.

00:01:20.579 --> 00:01:22.815
If he backed into your car
in the parking lot,

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:24.550
he would leave a note
on the windshield that said,

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:25.951
"I won't pay for repairs,

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:28.354
but here's a wallet-sized
portrait of me."

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:32.058
Signed, "Donald Trump.
I did nothing wrong."

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.993
Now, if you're
a Democratic primary voter,

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:35.161
I know what you're thinking.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.495
You've been watching
the rampant corruption

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:37.764
of the Trump presidency,

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.932
the catastrophic failure
of the Trump administration,

00:01:39.932 --> 00:01:41.267
and the destructive influence

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.702
the wealthy have had
on politics.

00:01:42.702 --> 00:01:44.436
And you're saying to yourself,
"You know what can fix this?

00:01:44.436 --> 00:01:46.639
A different rich guy."

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.607
Because if we've learned
one thing from the past decade

00:01:48.607 --> 00:01:51.911
of politics from the financial
crisis to the Trump presidency,

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.080
it's that rich people
with zero exceptions

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.281
know what they're doing.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.317
That's why they always do
smart, sane things

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.018
like leaving all their money
to their cats

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:03.389
or going on a podcast
and smoking weed like Elon Musk.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:06.359
That's the CEO of
a multibillion-dollar company,

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.828
and he looks like a 10th grader
at a sleepover.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.830
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:12.164
[ Stoned voice ]
Welcome to the board meeting.

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:14.601
First over of business.
We're going to build a rocket...

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:18.637
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.637 --> 00:02:20.539
...to White Castle.

00:02:20.539 --> 00:02:25.778
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.213
[ Normal voice ]
If you've been waiting for

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.215
a billionaire alternative,
your prayers have been answered

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.649
because a billionaire
is reportedly close

00:02:30.649 --> 00:02:32.384
to entering the race --
a billionaire so charming

00:02:32.384 --> 00:02:34.987
and charismatic,
whose Spanish is so perfect,

00:02:34.987 --> 00:02:36.922
no one will be able
to resist him.

00:02:36.922 --> 00:02:39.525
-Breaking news tonight.
The bombshell just dropping

00:02:39.525 --> 00:02:42.328
in the 2020 race --
Michael Bloomberg on the brink

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.597
of entering the Democratic
primary battle.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.532
-A spokesperson says Bloomberg
is worried

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.734
the current crop
of Democratic candidates

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:52.138
may not be able to defeat
President Trump.

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.173
But a recent poll also shows
that if Bloomberg

00:02:54.173 --> 00:02:55.475
were to enter the race,

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:57.877
only 6 percent
of Democratic primary voters

00:02:57.877 --> 00:02:59.879
say they'd definitely
vote for him.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.648
-Bloomberg was the Republican
mayor of New York City.

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:05.785
Now he's running as a Democrat.
How does he fit in?

00:03:05.785 --> 00:03:07.020
-Well, he'd run as a moderate.

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:08.754
And he would run on his record
as mayor.

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:11.457
-While in office, he had
a tendency to read statements

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:14.193
at the end of his press
conferences in Español.

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:20.466
-[ Speaking Spanish ]

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:22.067
<i> -iAy, caramba!</i>

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:25.705
Miguel Bloomberg esta
running for presidente!

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.840
<i> iAy, dios mío!</i>

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.910
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:34.513
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.513 --> 00:03:36.815
That's right.
Michael Bloomberg is reportedly

00:03:36.815 --> 00:03:38.651
close to jumping into
the Democratic primary.

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:40.019
You know, the guy who
used to be a Democrat,

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.887
then switched to Republican
to run for mayor,

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:44.223
then switched to Independent
after he became mayor,

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:45.524
then went back to
being a Democrat.

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:47.860
I mean, that's how my mom
orders at a restaurant.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.729
I'll have the fish --
No, the chicken.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:53.433
You know what? Just do me last.
Do me last.

00:03:53.433 --> 00:03:56.168
In reality, the vast majority
of Democratic primary voters

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:58.537
are saying in polls
that they're actually satisfied

00:03:58.537 --> 00:03:59.806
with the choices
they already have.

00:03:59.806 --> 00:04:02.074
In fact, there's already
another billionaire in the race,

00:04:02.074 --> 00:04:03.843
Tom Steyer. Remember him?

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.911
The guy who looks like
even he's surprised

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:08.380
he's running for president?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:09.848
He looks like a middle-aged dad

00:04:09.848 --> 00:04:12.185
who found his kid's acid
and accidentally ate it.

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:17.155
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.155 --> 00:04:20.826
I cannot see my hands.

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.962
And that wolf is talking to me.

00:04:22.962 --> 00:04:25.597
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.597 --> 00:04:27.600
And just...
[ Applause ]

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.437
Just to give you an idea of how
uninterested Democrats are

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:32.872
in having another
billionaire president,

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:35.975
Steyer has remained mired in the
low single digits in the polls

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:38.177
despite the fact that he spent
$47 million

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.979
during the first three months
of his presidential bid --

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.280
$47 million!

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.448
Instead of running for
president,

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.316
he could have funded
grassroots organizing

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:47.286
or just offered that same money
to Donald Trump to quit.

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:49.188
[ Laughter ]
You know Trump would take it.

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:51.724
If Trump knew someone would
be willing to pay him to resign,

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:53.326
he would probably start airing
infomercials

00:04:53.326 --> 00:04:56.228
with the hotline,
"1-800-1-MAKE-ME-AN-OFFER."

00:04:56.228 --> 00:04:58.864
[ As Trump ] Call now
and you can pay me to shut up.

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:00.065
And if the price is right,

00:05:00.065 --> 00:05:02.568
I'll throw in a second
even dumber Donald Trump.

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.036
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.036 --> 00:05:07.740
[ Normal voice ] So there just
doesn't seem to be an appetite

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:09.575
right now for another
billionaire president

00:05:09.575 --> 00:05:12.011
to swoop in and save us from the
current Democratic candidates.

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:13.712
People want to
change the system,

00:05:13.712 --> 00:05:16.215
but it's hard to convince
someone that a system broken

00:05:16.215 --> 00:05:18.918
when that system gave them
billions of dollars.

00:05:18.918 --> 00:05:20.586
Remember the futile campaign

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.221
of Starbucks founder
Howard Schultz?

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:23.856
He couldn't even announce
his candidacy

00:05:23.856 --> 00:05:25.157
without getting yelled at.

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:27.994
-Former Starbucks CEO
Howard Schultz got an earful

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:30.295
from a protestor at
a New York City book signing

00:05:30.295 --> 00:05:31.964
Monday night after Schultz said

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:34.534
he is seriously considering
a possible Independent run

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:37.603
for the White House.
-I am seriously considering

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:41.207
running for President
as a centrist Independent.

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:43.709
And I wanted to clarify the word
"Independent,"

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:48.747
which I view merely as
a designation on the ballot.

00:05:48.747 --> 00:05:51.484
-Don't help elect Trump,

00:05:51.484 --> 00:05:55.721
you egotistical
billionaire [bleep]

00:05:55.721 --> 00:05:58.391
-That's what you get

00:05:58.391 --> 00:06:01.727
for announcing your campaign
in New York City.

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:03.362
[ New York accent ]
Hey, Schultz, how about you take

00:06:03.362 --> 00:06:05.464
one of those cake pops
and stick it up your a--

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:06.965
Let's go, Mets!

00:06:06.965 --> 00:06:09.101
[ Laughter, cheers,
and applause ]

00:06:09.101 --> 00:06:12.672
Now billionaires...

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:14.140
Billionaires are apparently
worried

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.208
about the leftward tilt
of the current primary,

00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:17.709
and in particular,
the candidacies

00:06:17.709 --> 00:06:19.312
of Elizabeth Warren
and Bernie Sanders.

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:21.947
In fact, it was reported
Bloomberg had been coaxed

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:23.849
by another even wealthier
billionaire.

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:26.719
Vox reported that Jeff Bezos
asked Michael Bloomberg

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:28.954
months ago if he'd consider
running for president.

00:06:28.954 --> 00:06:33.125
Wow! He just ordered up
a presidential candidate.

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:35.261
What level of Amazon Prime
is that?

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:37.629
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.629 --> 00:06:40.032
Bloomberg's interest in running
and Bezos' prodding

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:41.667
come after weeks
of billionaire freakouts

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:43.268
over the possibility that
someone who's critical

00:06:43.268 --> 00:06:45.705
of big banks and Wall Street,
like Warren or Bernie,

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:46.973
could get the Democratic
nomination.

00:06:46.973 --> 00:06:49.909
In fact, last week, even
Bill Gates expressed concern

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:52.811
about how much he personally
would have to pay in taxes

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:55.714
and joked that he might not
have that much left over.

00:06:55.714 --> 00:06:59.551
-You know, I've paid over
$10 billion in taxes.

00:06:59.551 --> 00:07:04.089
I paid more than anyone
in taxes.

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:07.159
But I'm glad to have pa--
You know,

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:10.830
if I had to pay $20 billion,
that's fine.

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:13.933
But, you know, when you say
I should pay $100 billion,

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:16.435
okay, then I'm starting
to do a little math

00:07:16.435 --> 00:07:19.304
about what I have left over.

00:07:19.304 --> 00:07:20.872
Sorry, I'm just kidding.

00:07:20.872 --> 00:07:22.909
-First of all,
I think you got your math wrong

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:25.411
which makes sense because
you probably used Excel.

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:27.880
Secondly, we know you're kidding

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.748
because you have incredible
comic delivery

00:07:29.748 --> 00:07:32.818
and because you're worth
over $100 billion.

00:07:32.818 --> 00:07:34.620
If Elizabeth Warren
got elected president,

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:36.388
no one thinks Bill Gates
would be doing math

00:07:36.388 --> 00:07:38.457
on the back of a napkin
at his kitchen table,

00:07:38.457 --> 00:07:40.693
"Let's see, $6 billion
in wealth taxes

00:07:40.693 --> 00:07:43.028
another $10 billion
in income taxes.

00:07:43.028 --> 00:07:44.663
Oh, that leaves me
with $90 bil--

00:07:44.663 --> 00:07:46.432
That's barely enough
to survive!"

00:07:46.432 --> 00:07:48.968
I'm already cutting my own hair!

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:50.936
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:56.375
Besides, even if Gates
did run out of money,

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:58.578
we know he would have
a successful career as a dancer,

00:07:58.578 --> 00:08:00.179
as we learned from
a press conference

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:02.148
announcing the launch
of Windows 95.

00:08:02.148 --> 00:08:03.949
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:05.817
It looks like your accountant's
Christmas party

00:08:05.817 --> 00:08:08.153
after someone spikes the punch.

00:08:08.153 --> 00:08:10.489
That's the bar mitzvah
where the dads are trying to get

00:08:10.489 --> 00:08:14.026
the kids on the dance floor,
"Come on, guys!

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:16.095
We're doing the Macarena!"

00:08:16.095 --> 00:08:17.863
[ Claps ]

00:08:17.863 --> 00:08:20.199
Now, obviously Gates'
$100 billion tax estimate

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:21.467
was ridiculous. In fact,

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:23.302
to help him calculate
how much he'd owe in taxes

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:25.972
under her presidency,
Warren added a calculator

00:08:25.972 --> 00:08:28.307
for the billionaires to her
website with two custom links

00:08:28.307 --> 00:08:30.876
that say, "If you're
Michael Bloomberg, click here.

00:08:30.876 --> 00:08:33.579
And if you're Bill Gates,
you can click here."

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:36.682
Damn, she used the Internet
against Bill Gates.

00:08:36.682 --> 00:08:39.251
Next, she's gonna get Clippy
to endorse her.

00:08:39.251 --> 00:08:40.886
[ Laughter ]

00:08:40.886 --> 00:08:42.755
And Bill Gates isn't
the only billionaire

00:08:42.755 --> 00:08:44.256
freaking out about
Warren's candidacy.

00:08:44.256 --> 00:08:47.759
Last week, JPMorgan Chase CEO
Jamie Dimon criticized Warren

00:08:47.759 --> 00:08:49.161
for vilifying rich people.

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:51.297
-She uses some pretty harsh
words,

00:08:51.297 --> 00:08:54.166
some would say vilifies
successful people.

00:08:54.166 --> 00:08:55.634
I don't like vilifying anybody.

00:08:55.634 --> 00:08:58.470
I think we should applaud
successful people.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:02.308
-You have a billion dollars,
and you also want applause?

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:03.842
I thought the whole point
of being rich

00:09:03.842 --> 00:09:05.844
was not having to care
what people think of you.

00:09:05.844 --> 00:09:07.513
That's why they call it
"[Bleep] you" money,

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:10.082
not "[Bleep] you,
now give me a hug" money.

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:11.516
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.516 --> 00:09:13.586
Dimon was also on "60 Minutes"
on Sunday.

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:15.854
Dimon was asked about his salary
last year,

00:09:15.854 --> 00:09:17.990
which came out to $31 million.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.724
He was also pressed on
whether he took

00:09:19.724 --> 00:09:21.159
any responsibility at all

00:09:21.159 --> 00:09:23.329
for JPMorgan's role
in the financial crisis,

00:09:23.329 --> 00:09:25.565
which, of course,
is one of the major reasons

00:09:25.565 --> 00:09:27.266
voters are so angry
at Wall Street.

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:29.234
And he changed his answer
within seconds.

00:09:29.234 --> 00:09:32.737
-Do you take any responsibility
for the financial crisis

00:09:32.737 --> 00:09:34.239
in 2008?
-No.

00:09:34.239 --> 00:09:36.809
-But your bank sold
those same kind of mortgages.

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:40.179
-We -- Yeah. I do take some.

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:42.948
-He's dancing around that
question like Bill Gates in '95.

00:09:42.948 --> 00:09:44.850
[ Laughter ]

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.453
People aren't just mad
at billionaires out of jealousy

00:09:47.453 --> 00:09:48.887
or because candidates demonize
them.

00:09:48.887 --> 00:09:50.188
There are real world examples

00:09:50.188 --> 00:09:52.124
that are informing
people's doubts

00:09:52.124 --> 00:09:53.558
that the wealthy can solve
everything.

00:09:53.558 --> 00:09:54.694
Just take Mark Zuckerberg.

00:09:54.694 --> 00:09:56.295
Facebook recently announced

00:09:56.295 --> 00:09:57.729
that it won't fact-check
political ads.

00:09:57.729 --> 00:09:58.831
And Zuckerberg was grilled

00:09:58.831 --> 00:10:00.966
by Congresswoman
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez

00:10:00.966 --> 00:10:03.369
about that decision recently,
he had no answers.

00:10:03.369 --> 00:10:06.305
-You announced recently that
the official policy of Facebook

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:10.175
now allows politicians to pay to
spread disinformation

00:10:10.175 --> 00:10:13.112
in 2020 elections
and in the future.

00:10:13.112 --> 00:10:16.248
So I just want to know
how far I can push this.

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:19.051
Would I be able to run
advertisements on Facebook

00:10:19.051 --> 00:10:20.752
targeting Republicans
in primaries

00:10:20.752 --> 00:10:23.089
saying that they voted
for the Green New Deal?

00:10:23.089 --> 00:10:24.422
I mean,
if you're not fact-checking

00:10:24.422 --> 00:10:26.292
political advertisements,
I'm just trying to understand

00:10:26.292 --> 00:10:28.594
the bounds here,
what's fair game.

00:10:28.594 --> 00:10:30.195
-Congresswoman, I, uh --

00:10:30.195 --> 00:10:32.097
I don't know the answer to that
off the top of my head.

00:10:32.097 --> 00:10:34.032
-Do you see
a potential problem here

00:10:34.032 --> 00:10:35.901
with the complete lack
of fact-checking

00:10:35.901 --> 00:10:38.037
on political advertisements?

00:10:38.037 --> 00:10:40.439
-Well, Congressman,
I think lying is bad,

00:10:40.439 --> 00:10:42.707
and I think if you were to
run an ad that had a lie,

00:10:42.707 --> 00:10:44.876
that would be bad.
-Oh, really?

00:10:44.876 --> 00:10:46.912
[ Laughter ]
Would that be bad?

00:10:46.912 --> 00:10:49.548
So if I said you didn't
look like cross

00:10:49.548 --> 00:10:51.951
between Data from Star Trek
and a teenage roman emperor,

00:10:51.951 --> 00:10:54.086
that would be bad?

00:10:54.086 --> 00:10:55.954
So the billionaires
are freaking out

00:10:55.954 --> 00:10:57.389
about Warren and Bernie,
but neither of them

00:10:57.389 --> 00:10:58.824
seem especially worried
about it.

00:10:58.824 --> 00:11:00.926
Earlier this year, when Warren
was asked about the reaction

00:11:00.926 --> 00:11:02.494
among billionaires
to her candidacy,

00:11:02.494 --> 00:11:04.829
she had only
a sarcastic response.

00:11:04.829 --> 00:11:07.499
-They're gonna throw everything
at you to stop you.

00:11:07.499 --> 00:11:11.036
How do you get
from here to there?

00:11:11.036 --> 00:11:12.938
[ Laughter ]

00:11:12.938 --> 00:11:15.641
-Are you telling me that the
billionaires are not in favor

00:11:15.641 --> 00:11:18.043
of my being president
of the United States?

00:11:18.043 --> 00:11:19.578
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:19.578 --> 00:11:22.047
Damn, you just upset
every plan I had.

00:11:22.047 --> 00:11:24.183
[ Laughter ]
I'm shocked!

00:11:24.183 --> 00:11:26.785
-Sarcastic Elizabeth Warren
is like the teacher

00:11:26.785 --> 00:11:29.421
catching you smoking out back
behind the high school.

00:11:29.421 --> 00:11:32.158
Wow! Smoking is so cool!

00:11:32.158 --> 00:11:34.493
Do you know what else
is cool? Emphysema.

00:11:34.493 --> 00:11:35.727
[ Laughter ]

00:11:35.727 --> 00:11:37.997
You know the girls like
yellow teeth and skin.

00:11:37.997 --> 00:11:39.732
All right. I'll see you guys
back in class.

00:11:39.732 --> 00:11:41.367
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.367 --> 00:11:42.668
Then there's Bernie.
Last month,

00:11:42.668 --> 00:11:45.537
Bernie went on CNBC to make
the case that Wall Street

00:11:45.537 --> 00:11:47.473
should pay more to reduce
income inequality.

00:11:47.473 --> 00:11:51.009
And at one point, he referred
to his "friends on Wall Street."

00:11:51.009 --> 00:11:54.746
-At a time of massive income
and wealth inequality,

00:11:54.746 --> 00:11:57.549
it is my view that
the wealthiest people

00:11:57.549 --> 00:11:59.784
in this country,
the top 1/10 of 1%,

00:11:59.784 --> 00:12:01.253
should be paying
substantially more

00:12:01.253 --> 00:12:02.287
than they're paying right now.

00:12:02.287 --> 00:12:04.322
You have an insane situation.

00:12:04.322 --> 00:12:07.326
I let my Wall Street
friends there

00:12:07.326 --> 00:12:08.694
tell me why it makes sense.

00:12:08.694 --> 00:12:10.429
-You have Wall Street friends?
-No, I don't.

00:12:10.429 --> 00:12:12.331
That was just a metaph--
[ Laughter ]

00:12:12.331 --> 00:12:14.099
I was trying to sound nice.
I don't.

00:12:14.099 --> 00:12:16.302
-Of course Bernie doesn't have
Wall Street friends.

00:12:16.302 --> 00:12:17.736
I'm guessing that unless
you're a member

00:12:17.736 --> 00:12:20.139
of the Vermont Food Co-op
or the Burlington Y,

00:12:20.139 --> 00:12:22.274
you're not friends with Bernie
at all.

00:12:22.274 --> 00:12:24.143
[ As Sanders ]
I go swimming at 5:00 a.m.,

00:12:24.143 --> 00:12:25.443
and then I do a shift
at the co-op,

00:12:25.443 --> 00:12:27.146
and then I go home
and I don't talk to anybody.

00:12:27.146 --> 00:12:28.680
[ Laughter ]

00:12:28.680 --> 00:12:30.816
[ Normal voice ] And I'm glad
Bernie admitted that.

00:12:30.816 --> 00:12:32.517
Because if there's one thing
we've all learned

00:12:32.517 --> 00:12:33.819
from the billionaires,
it's that...

00:12:33.819 --> 00:12:35.621
-Lying is bad.
-Yeah.

00:12:35.621 --> 00:12:38.924
[ Laughter ]

00:12:38.924 --> 00:12:41.760
We're living in an unprecedented
era of massive inequality.

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:43.863
And there's an incredible hunger
among voters for a candidate

00:12:43.863 --> 00:12:45.563
who will fight for
a systemic change.

00:12:45.563 --> 00:12:46.965
Voters don't seem to want

00:12:46.965 --> 00:12:49.268
a self-appointed billionaire
savior to ride in and save them,

00:12:49.268 --> 00:12:51.269
and if you think
you are that savior,

00:12:51.269 --> 00:12:52.304
you might actually just be a...

00:12:52.304 --> 00:12:56.041
-Egotistical
billionaire [bleep]

00:12:56.041 --> 00:12:58.877
-This has been "A Closer Look."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:58.877 --> 00:13:00.880 line:0%
♪♪

